    {
      "label": "Continental Expands Portfolio of Large and High-Performance Tires September 16, 2026 Continental has significantly expanded its global portfolio of ultra-high-performance (UHP) tires – tires measuring 18 inches and above – over the past five years and plans to strengthen this segment further in the future. By the end of 2027, the company will add more than 650 new tire sizes across all tire lines, for both original equipment on new cars and the replacement market. By expanding its portfolio, the tire manufacturer is responding to growing demand for high-performance tires designed for larger, heavier and more powerful vehicles, as well as electrified drive systems, while laying the foundation for further profitable growth in this segment. Find out more",
      "href": "/en/press/press-releases/ultra-high-performance-tires/"
    },
    {
      "label": "Porsche Chooses Continental Tires September 29, 2026 Continental has received two new approvals to supply original-equipment tires for Porsche models. The automotive manufacturer has approved both the SportContact 7 and the new SportContact 7 Force for the Panamera G3 II. The SportContact 7 Force is a high-performance addition to Continental’s summer tire line. Porsche also recommends the WinterContact TS 860 S for the Cayenne E4 during the colder months. Find out more",
      "href": "/en/press/press-releases/oe-porsche/"
    },
    {
      "label": "Safe Through Ice and Snow: Continental Expands Conti Scandinavia Winter Tire Portfolio September 15, 2026 Continental is expanding its Conti Scandinavia winter tire portfolio with a new 315/60 R 22.5 steering axle tire. Find out more",
      "href": "/en/press/press-releases/20260915-winter/"
    },
    {
      "label": "Continental Develops Concept Tire Containing Over 40 Percent Recycled Materials for EU Project August 25, 2026 As part of the EU-funded ZEvRA project, Continental has developed a concept tire made from around 43 percent recycled materials. The concept tire highlights the potential of innovative material approaches. It also demonstrates the need for a reliable framework when adopting recycling technologies on an industrial scale. Find out more",
      "href": "/en/press/press-releases/eu-project-zevra/"
    },
